 "why_the_backgrounds_disagree": {
  "explanation": "AVI is a whole-genome pathogenicity score and ranks amino-acid-changing variants highly. Against a whole-locus background its top slice is filled by coding positions, which leaves few places for non-coding positives. Restricting the background to non-coding positions removes that competition. The disagreement between the two comparisons is therefore a property of the question asked, not an artefact.",
